seg-10f79909a5bc = <b>The Celeste IOD (in-orbit demonstration) preset is optional.</b> Its signal parameters were presented at the European Space Agency (ESA) Navigation Innovation and Support Programme (NAVISP) LEO-PNT workshop, { "2026" }, and have no public source yet; they live in the <c1/> module of <c2/>, used by <c3/>. How the preset is withheld: every workshop-derived number of the engine lives in one file, <c4/>, which <c5/> compiles in only when it exists, and in the repository-only scenarios <c6/>. Deleting that file and those scenarios withholds the preset with no source edit; every other test, oracle and scenario runs without it, and the README's scenario-file count still counts the withheld files. Its EIRP and beam are calibrated to a C/N0 trace shown at the workshop, so that scenario reproduces the trace by construction.

