seg-91941393400a = The optional <c1/> section counterfeits the signals a receiver would see at a claimed position. From <c2/> the claimed position jumps by <c3/> and then moves horizontally at <c4/> toward <c5/>; the counterfeit range and range rate are exactly those of the claimed position, on the LEO bands named in <c6/> (default all) and on the MEO GNSS signal unless <c7/>. <c8/> says whether the counterfeit pseudoranges carry the ionospheric delay (a ground transmitter's do not).

